## What this predicate means

**A `uses-method-in` B** — artifact A (memoir / library / decision / synthesis / etc.) employs a method, technique, or framework specified by B (pattern / protocol).  The methodology-citation typed-edge.  Distinguishes from `evidences` (witness/example), from `cites` (weak external pointer), and from `implements` (full spec realization) — `uses-method-in` is "this artifact employed that methodology as part of its construction."

